msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:14
#: 97856559541848fea615f99d8f484d57
msgid "This article provides an overview of the :ref:`PX4FMU <common-px4fmu-overview>` and :ref:`PX4IO <common-px4io-overview>` Board Plane Wiring/Installation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:18
#: 53047151a7cb4a92b5f1a8213455780a
msgid "PX4FMU plus PX4IO Wiring Diagram for Plane"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:27
#: 5d2d9abffa134ca6b99fa39b15de9f90
msgid "Assembly"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:30
#: 503a4f52fe7f4fafba4e8694233a4ddb
msgid "**Solder the right angle 9x3 pin connector that was included with your PX4 kit to the side of the PX4IO board that has \"PX4 autopilot\" printed on it.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:34
#: ca515724b2b340b5a6c0eae7dab82f5f
msgid "When you insert the 9 x 3 connector into the PX4IO board put it in with the plastic spacer on the connector facing to the back of the board, NOT down against the board."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:38
#: c2de1d968241481791da679b960de191
msgid "**Solder the small white PAP-02-VS 2 pin connector into the 2 holes directly behind the battery pads on the PX4IO board.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:40
#: 331fad013bb14a12919ac355fde9caed
msgid "**Install the PX4IO board on top of the PX4FMU board.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:42
#: f37a163e0b2c4f82a7cd715ddce1e0bf
msgid "Ensure all of the connector pins are straight and insertion is complete."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:44
#: 3d42ace07485485da6f62f4ff72a101d
msgid "Mount the PX4-FMU + PX4-IO board stack in a central and level location on top of your Plane."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:46
#: 897f06aa8b9944fca608bf2a86af0fcd
msgid "The PX4FMU board is normally on top."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:47
#: e91233cc58bd4f83811e9b89fa923fac
msgid "It can be advantageous to mount the PX4IO board on top to provide for better Connector access."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:49
#: 677c8864ccdf44c0b5e450d73dce4752
msgid "If you do mount the PX4IO board on top it will be necessary to set the \"Board Orientation (AHRS_ORIENTATION)\" parameter to \"Roll 180\" in the Advanced Parameter List in Mission Planner."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:52
#: 2fd38e6930184e46a3589f86078f3611
msgid "The arrow labeled \"FRONT\" should be facing to the front of the aircraft."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:54
#: 5295473b0da341a8a84bfa3d1da7806c
msgid "The Micro SD memory card holder should face to the back of the Aircraft."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:57
#: b19c69e7212a4c8cacd58703effedd6e
msgid "**Use the included standoffs and hardware.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:59
#: bd57bc4ace3f446f911bb676e69b9919
msgid "Which ever side of which ever board is going to be on top but a black standoff through one of the mounting holes from the bottom and thread a black plastic nut onto it from the top."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:62
#: e3269e297cd44364890e01b58c01b187
msgid "Repeat the above for the remaining 3 holes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:63
#: d57ca4c624c8449197502ec1f84c3191
msgid "Connect the PX4FMU and PX4IO board insuring no pins are bent on the board interconnection connector."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:65
#: 26861a9d86704f21b6440bea8ea458fe
msgid "Thread 4 more of the black standoffs into the already installed black standoffs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:68
#: bae715d36a9144c28be32c1ee314d3bf
msgid "**You will need additional vibration damping and you should also review the Wiki section on vibration control.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:71
#: 7eb6a87a1cdd4479a6323b9a44af9321
msgid "At a minimum you should mount the standoffs to an intermediate plate."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:73
#: 2cda5b699265442b9da219fe05727cf3
msgid "Mount the plate to your airframe with 4 small (<1\")square pads of Kyosho \"Zeal\" gel or \"Moon Gel\" in the corners."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:76
#: cfe643aaf93143ecbc21823fb1630bfe
msgid "**Mount the GPS facing up with an unobstructed \"view\" of the sky.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:78
#: b0049ff15d2048678b773b69a7f1a985
msgid "Connect the GPS cable to the GPS connector on the PX4FMU board."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:79
#: 6222a8c12b8a4465925ca2cacb159252
msgid "The GPS must be positioned so that its cable will connect without strain to the PX4FMU's GPS connector."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:81
#: da5c9e37675f47d391bd2e08cea2bf48
msgid "The GPS can be mounted on a short riser to give it the widest satellite access."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:86
#: d89115b6809b4c4ab4a7a6370bb15f66
msgid "Wire the PX4FMU and PX4IO boards to Your Plane"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:88
#: 8388a7bc72304e6596986989e1049d4a
msgid "**Wire the PX4-IO board.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:90
#: 5845f12b35d94f348acda8167969d9d1
msgid "The PX4IO board has a built in Power Supply which can connect to up to 18 volts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:92
#: 6d00a9e0c6474fb4b03138adfb6d61ce
msgid "Insert the white PAP-02-VS 2 pin connector with the black and red wires coming out of it into the mating power connector you soldered in previously on the PX4IO board."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:95
#: aa6e662a334d42108b367a97c231c765
msgid "Battery Plus is the(red wire) and should be soldered to your battery red power lead / connector."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:97
#: e37e52a329724505994c909eb278a046
msgid "Battery Ground is the(black wire) and should be soldered to your battery black battery (Ground) lead / connector."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:99
#: 2a3bdc7a91c449708d46dd6c6a3f51f8
msgid "The main power inputs of your ESC's will also need to connect to these wires and to a battery connector."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:101
#: 1f04d4fc08f14971a0244fce832a50fb
msgid "A Power Distribution board can also be used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:103
#: 452b2a05f3484ed78d22514804803f5c
msgid "**Connect your PPM-Sum RC receiver's 3 wire cable to the end of the 9 x 3 angle connector that is nearest the edge of the PX4IO board with the signal wire furthest from the board and the ground closest to the board.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:107
#: a4cae3db4dcd48a782b7df2356ffd632
msgid "**Wire the PX4 boards servo out signals to your Servo / ESC control inputs.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:110
#: a924bfdb9e8e4af99e9546dff578be59
msgid "The ESCs BEC or a separate UBEC can supply servo power to the Servos via the PX4's Servo connector BUS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:113
#: 22fbdb94137b4b48a5a1607fe251475a
msgid "Run the 3 wire servo cables from the ESC (and its built in BEC) and Servos to the 3 x 9 Servo Connector on the PX4IO board."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:115
#: e9cea0ecf1ea4e0bbc98d7f8496b36c0
msgid "Or, clip the power lead on the ESC and run power and ground from a separate UBEC to the bottom pins of the Servo connector."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:118
#: 4b6a53edeb1040f28dac2dc8ffaeda0a
msgid "The PX4IO board connector for Servo 1 is at the edge of the connector next to the Battery power in wires."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:120
#: a9bb32646c7747c18783fc389ac129e4
msgid "Insert the Servo and Motor ESC signal wires arranged progressively from that edge, (1,2,3,4,etc)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:122
#: bbbd779043474254a95604bd851b46c4
msgid "You can put the ESC / Servo Signal wires into a single inline connector with the correct number of pins for your Plane."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:124
#: 26a393c6e4bb44bb84b2fa724b5dbcbd
msgid "The ESC / Servo Signal Wires / connector should be plugged into the top row (furthest from the board) of the PX4IO boards 3 x 9 Servo Connector."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:128
#: d3cb9971a8d74996b100af17bf70a8bb
msgid "**Note, the cable that is supplied in the plastic envelope with the UBLOX GPS which has white 6 pin connectors on both ends is not the correct cable for the PX4FMU board.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:132
#: 7db385f4b7a3443caba38fb4022d291a
msgid "The correct longer cable is provided in a separate envelope and has a 5 pin \"beige\" connector on one end and a 6 pin white connector on the other end."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:135
#: 893c2dceaf0d46949d720669256303ce
msgid "Plug the correct GPS cable's white 6 pin connector into the 6 pin socket on the GPS."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:137
#: 9b74116b2ee64e6a93c930d1780d2bb0
msgid "Plug the beige 5 pin connector into the PX4FMU board's 5 pin GPS socket which is next to the 15 pin DF13 Mini connector."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:140
#: 866b4f42e40f458fa82e6bc160acaef2
msgid "**Plug the 2 pin connector attached to the lead supplied with the buzzer into the buzzer socket on the side of the PX4FMU board that has the SD card holder on it.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:143
#: 3a492d4003044ae086fb41e15c3d5c63
msgid "**Connect the \"Safety Button\" to the Safety button connector on the PX4IO board on the opposite side of the board from the Battery pads.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:147
#: 62879dde89244469becaa840c17d2217
msgid "**The PX4 must have its \"Safety\" mechanism disengaged before it can be armed.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:150
#: 25884dda7fd146b08f80312888c9ea57
msgid "**PX4 Safety Button LED Indications:**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:152
#: 247d3a6c3e5945cdaf0eafa55f845de3
msgid "Fast Blinking indicates: Error Condition, Safety cannot be disengaged. Possibly not calibrated or sensor error."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:154
#: 96b77b4cb46145e887008c265aad9ecf
msgid "Slow Blinking indicates: Safe condition. Safety can be disengaged by depressing Safety Button for 5 seconds."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:156
#: fd07cd014d724c6c957a5981ae1b7909
msgid "LED Continuously on indicates: Safety has been disengaged. Depending on your parameter settings, throttle may be armed with Throttle down and to the right.  For details on arming see: :ref:`Arming Plane <arming-your-plane>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:160
#: ae81076973d249c88607c84fbf02799d
msgid "When the LED is continuously on indicating Safety Disengaged it may be toggled back to a Safety engaged condition by depressing the Safety button for 5 seconds."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:164
#: 93d34d7734a340c08d0a480a969cc3e6
msgid "**Both the Safety engaged and Safety disengaged conditions require the button to be held down for 5 seconds to toggle them.**. This is a safety mechanism to prevent accidental disarming during flight and accidental arming during transportation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:170
#: b90b25f625c849fd96261239237b945d
msgid "Using a SiK telemetry radio with your PX4FMU plus PX4IO system."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:172
#: e4a2543a41cc4d07ad8712488cc798a6
msgid "You will need a :ref:`SiK Radio <common-sik-telemetry-radio>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:173
#: dddbda2208fb4dc1afd12fdab09f6896
msgid "Plug the telemetry adapter cable's large black connector into the SiK Radio as shown above."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:175
#: 3935fb9519dd41cdb381fb9750d3758c
msgid "The telemetry radio is shown above **incorrectly** connected to the FMU USART2 socket at the corner of the PX4IO board."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:178
#: 051fd6fcc98f4b74aad4a6f25ffc9e1c
msgid "**Correctly** plug the telemetry adapter cable's beige connector into the PX4IO boards **FMU UART5** socket."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:180
#: 57521c60b6cd4ee0bf792cee7f0d0cb4
msgid "FMU UART5 is the middle socket on the end of the PX4IO board as indicated by the **red arrow** above."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:182
#: 404f6a45eebd4c66aa93d3e31e1cbe91
msgid "(FMU UARTx) means a port that is pass through connected directly from the PX4IO board to the PX4FMU."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:186
#: 718b917e240642f3a4ad66a3ef49bf41
msgid "Separate Servo power for high power applications"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:191
#: a847f85ae8c64c6eba200e4732e5847c
msgid "**Using a separate power supply to provide power to the center servo power pins of the PX4IO board.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:194
#: 8b48fa9a13de4937a99041fa8c75659e
msgid "If you are driving high power servos with your PX4IO board you will want to provide servo power separately."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:196
#: fd412bb131fb498ab798cffe7f283a0c
msgid "In order to do this, remove the L1 Ferrite device circled in red on the image above."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:198
#: f28c86dda0b64989b955c7b6d09b9e74
msgid "Then run power from your separate power supply to one of the center pins of the Servo Connector."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:200
#: c2239fa063cb43f08805b056a066d0ef
msgid "And run the ground from your separate power supply to one of the servo connector pins nearest the edge of the board."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:204
#: 7ea1ad4e9b0a4562a7a632329fbd77e3
msgid "Using a Standard RC Radio Receiver with an 8 channel PPM Encoder"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:207
#: 5d0cc58e89b245af923e56a7b76dc003
msgid "**You can use a standard radio receiver with an 8 channel PPM Encoder in place of the PPM-SUM receiver.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:210
#: 5e1a048757ec46b7866f083d98c89d40
msgid "An 8 Channel PPM Encoder is `available from jDrones here <http://store.jdrones.com/pixhawk_px4_paparazzi_ppm_encoder_v2_p/eleppmenc20.htm>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:212
#: b2b9fa66c05e43dca14520867d59267f
msgid "Solder a 3x8 Right angle connector from the top into one end of the 8 Channel PPM Encoder board."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:214
#: 503a443592a047c2bb786c3633bea71c
msgid "With the 3x8 connector up and facing away from you, solder a 3x1 Right angle connector on the right edge of the 8 Channel PPM Encoder board."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:218
#: af30b9d0ab65441986b865dc2addd48d
msgid "**Connect 5-8 output channels of your receiver to the inputs of the 8 Channel Encoder (signal wire furthest from board) with 5-8 female to female servo jumpers.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:222
#: e76660b3e6b34a3881100ac837f120d6
msgid "Connect the PPM-SUM output of the Encoder with a 3 wire cable to the PX4IO boards PPM sum input (1x3 connector)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:227
#: 86dba9883dee4d90b2c8a67ebc79425b
msgid "If you are using a 3DR PPM Encoder it is important to know that when you are calibrating your transmitter you will quite likely need to hook up your flight battery to the PX4IO because the USB port alone can't supply enough power."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:233
#: 7e151a42361249a889f4db20a5d9da55
msgid "Compatible remote control (RC) receivers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:235
#: 478e8d94bc5941cfae0c1362bcc47d10
msgid "PX4 is compatible with PPM remote control (RC) receivers, Futaba S.Bus receivers, and Spektrum DSM,DSM2, and DSM-X Satellite receivers. For traditional single-wire-per-channel (PWM) receivers a PPM encoder can be used to convert the receiver outputs to PPM-SUM.  Information about compatible receivers and how they are connected can be found in :ref:`this wiki page <common-rc-systems>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-plus-px4io-wiring.rst:244
#: 9abbc7aaf1c24c68982348422afda953
msgid "FRSky Taranis Transmitter"
msgstr ""
